{# header/main_navigation/footer carry access: authenticated in
   config/settings.info.yaml's regions: list, so they already render as ''
   for a logged-out visitor (Kernel::renderRegion()) -- no route-name check
   needed here at all, unlike the version this replaced. The only thing
   left to derive is whether to add wrapper-bare, purely so .login-page's
   own CSS knows there's no header/footer around it to leave room for
   (web/css/styles.css's .wrapper-bare .login-page rule). #}
{# live_edit (zeusfw core/modules/live_edit/) -- Step 1 of a planned
   live-editing feature, a small block showing which .zetem template the
   current page's content came from. No region of its own (same reasoning
   accessibility/google_analytics already document), so it's invoked ad
   hoc here rather than through the regions: loop below. Gated by both
   live_edit_enabled (true here -- content-live-edit is a new, narrow
   permission nobody but doctor/maintenance/is_superuser holds, see
   web/rbac_seed.php) and rbacClass::isPermitted(ZEUSFW_PERM_LIVE_EDIT) --
   renders '' for anyone else, including a logged-out visitor.

   Placed first, before the wrapper/regions below -- deliberately in normal
   document flow now, not position:fixed (see live_edit.css's own comment
   for why: this app's own chrome likely establishes a containing block
   that breaks position:fixed children, the same class of bug
   accessibility's own CLAUDE.md entry documents). Pushing the rest of the
   page down a row is an accepted, temporary trade-off while this is being
   tried out. #}
{{ module('live_edit', ['enabled' => true]) }}
{% $__bareLayout = trim(($regions['header'] ?? '') . ($regions['main_navigation'] ?? '') . ($regions['footer'] ?? '')) === ''; %}
<div class="wrapper{% if($__bareLayout): %} wrapper-bare{% endif %}">
    {% foreach($regions as $reg): %}
        {{ $reg }}
    {% endforeach %}
</div>
